1
00:00:00,091 --> 00:00:01,651
A single sentence in your journal.

2
00:00:02,031 --> 00:00:03,231
The goal is not the result.

3
00:00:03,651 --> 00:00:05,111
The goal is to become the kind of

4
00:00:05,111 --> 00:00:06,291
person who shows up.

5
00:00:06,511 --> 00:00:08,611
And that identity is built one tiny rep

6
00:00:08,611 --> 00:00:09,291
at a time.

7
00:00:09,631 --> 00:00:10,871
Small is not a compromise.

8
00:00:11,491 --> 00:00:12,651
Small is the strategy.

9
00:00:13,091 --> 00:00:14,911
Now let's talk about why this works.

10
00:00:15,351 --> 00:00:16,671
When a task feels huge,

11
00:00:17,111 --> 00:00:18,891
your brain focuses on the cost.

12
00:00:19,151 --> 00:00:21,711
It imagines the effort, the time, and the

13
00:00:21,711 --> 00:00:22,951
discomfort all at once.

14
00:00:22,951 --> 00:00:24,731
That is why we procrastinate.

15
00:00:25,191 --> 00:00:25,951
We are not lazy.

16
00:00:26,311 --> 00:00:27,131
We are overwhelmed.

17
00:00:27,591 --> 00:00:29,811
A tiny promise removes the overwhelm.

18
00:00:30,071 --> 00:00:32,071
It gives your brain a clear, easy next

19
00:00:32,071 --> 00:00:32,511
step.

20
00:00:32,831 --> 00:00:34,891
And once you take that step, the task

21
00:00:34,891 --> 00:00:36,291
stops being an abstraction.

22
00:00:36,791 --> 00:00:38,711
It becomes something you are already doing.

23
00:00:39,151 --> 00:00:40,951
This is why the first two minutes matter

24
00:00:40,951 --> 00:00:42,071
more than the last 20.

25
00:00:42,411 --> 00:00:44,171
The hardest part of any habit is the

26
00:00:44,171 --> 00:00:46,431
transition from thinking about it to doing it.

27
00:00:46,691 --> 00:00:48,651
There is a second benefit, and it is

28
00:00:48,651 --> 00:00:49,331
easy to miss.

29
00:00:49,711 --> 00:00:51,871
Small promises protect your identity.

30
00:00:51,871 --> 00:00:53,911
If you set a giant goal and fail,

31
00:00:54,251 --> 00:00:55,891
you start to believe you are the kind

32
00:00:55,891 --> 00:00:57,671
of person who cannot follow through.

33
00:00:58,131 --> 00:00:59,671
If you set a tiny goal and keep

34
00:00:59,671 --> 00:01:01,911
it, you build evidence that you are reliable.

35
00:01:02,311 --> 00:01:03,251
That evidence compounds.

36
00:01:03,831 --> 00:01:06,231
After a week, you have seven proofs.

37
00:01:06,371 --> 00:01:08,111
After a month, you have 30.

38
00:01:08,471 --> 00:01:10,051
The goal is not to impress anyone.

39
00:01:10,611 --> 00:01:12,311
The goal is to trust yourself again.

40
00:01:12,691 --> 00:01:14,131
So here is a simple practice.

41
00:01:14,671 --> 00:01:16,211
Choose one habit you care about.

42
00:01:16,591 --> 00:01:18,271
Cut it down until it takes less than

43
00:01:18,271 --> 00:01:18,891
five minutes.

44
00:01:19,271 --> 00:01:20,891
Do it at the same time every day.

45
00:01:20,891 --> 00:01:22,331
Mark it on a calendar.

46
00:01:22,751 --> 00:01:24,671
Do not increase the size until the habit

47
00:01:24,671 --> 00:01:25,571
feels automatic.

48
00:01:26,051 --> 00:01:27,431
Most people rush this step.

49
00:01:27,751 --> 00:01:29,371
They feel good for three days and then

50
00:01:29,371 --> 00:01:30,051
double the goal.

